prompts.research:
{{voice}}

SUBJECT: {{subject}}
{{angleLine}}
{{notes}}

{{pillars}}

Do the research for one cookbook on this subject. Real dishes, real methods, real
measurements. Prefer what a working cook would tell you over what a search result says.

Research tools are available to you. Use them, and record only sources you actually saw.

Return ONLY JSON:
{
  "title": "the book title - appetising, not descriptive, max 6 words",
  "thesis": "one sentence: the argument this book makes about how to cook this.",
  "technique":       [{"fact":"...","why_it_matters":"...","source":"URL you opened, or empty"}],
  "ingredient":      [{"fact":"...","choosing":"how to pick a good one","season":"...","source":"..."}],
  "origin":          [{"fact":"...","where":"...","contested":"what is disputed, or empty","source":"..."}],
  "science":         [{"idea":"...","the_number":"a real temperature, time or ratio","source":"..."}],
  "variation":       [{"dish":"...","what_changes":"...","source":"..."}],
  "troubleshooting": [{"problem":"...","cause":"...","fix":"...","source":"..."}],
  "uncertain": ["anything above you are not confident is accurate"]
}
6-10 entries per array. "uncertain" may be empty but must be honest.

prompts.page:
{{voice}}

You are writing ONE page of "{{title}}".
THESIS OF THE BOOK: {{thesis}}
{{notes}}
{{sectionLine}}
{{registerLine}}

PAGE {{pageNumber}} - "{{pageTitle}}"
type: {{pageType}} - density: {{pageDensity}} - pillar: {{pagePillar}}
premise: {{pagePremise}}
pages either side: {{neighbours}}

RESEARCH YOU MAY DRAW ON:
{{pageResearch}}
{{takenBlock}}
LENGTH: the body must be {{wordsLow}}-{{wordsHigh}} words. This is a hard constraint - the page is a
fixed physical area and overset copy cannot be placed.{{plateNote}}

If this page is a recipe, the body must contain, in this order: a one-line headnote,
the yield and total time, the ingredients with exact quantities in metric and cups,
then the numbered method. Every step names what the cook should observe, not just do.

Also write the VISUAL BRIEF. It is handed to an image generator verbatim, so it must
describe a photograph, not a concept: the dish or the hands, framing, light, surface,
palette, mood. No text or lettering anywhere in the image - the type is set separately.

Return ONLY JSON:
{
  "title": "final page title, may differ from the working one",
  "deck":  "the headnote - one sentence that makes the reader want to cook this.",
  "body":  "the page copy, plain prose or the recipe as described above",
  "pull_quote": "the one line worth setting large, taken from the body, or empty",
  "furniture": [{"kind":"caption|sidebar|stat|did-you-know|margin-note","text":"..."}],
  "image_prompt": "the visual brief, one paragraph, for the image generator",
  "image_orientation": "landscape|portrait|square",
  "sources": ["what this page's facts rest on - real, or empty if none"],
  "uncertain": ["anything here you are not confident is accurate"]
}
